== 2. The pop-up's own path: probe-popup.sh (Run) ==
With HANDOFF_TEST_POPUP naming a file, as well as HANDOFF_TEST_NOTIFY, handoff starts its
real pop-up process (_popup), and that process writes what it would hand the dialog to the
file, as "title | text | buttons", and is never clicked. So this is the text the operator
would see, not the alert's text in the notify log, which is what I read in round 3.
atterm_n.py answers decide's [y/N] with n.
(My first run of this probe also ran handoff on its own at a pty, which waits for input I
hadn't scripted; I stopped it and took that step out. No pop-up process was left running.)

